## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Nói to có ghi âm

**Chủ đề: khi nào nên memo hóa, và khi nào không.**

> *"Memoisation isn't free, and I think that's the part people skip.*
> *Every React.memo does a shallow comparison of all props on every parent render, and holds the previous result in memory. For a component that renders in a fraction of a millisecond and takes half a dozen props, the comparison can cost more than just re-rendering it.*
> *So my rule is: measure first. I memoise when the component is genuinely expensive to render, or when it's inside a long list where the same work repeats hundreds of times. Otherwise I leave it alone.*
> *There's also a trap where memo looks applied but does nothing. If the parent passes an inline arrow function as a prop, that's a new reference every render, so the shallow comparison always says "changed" and memo never kicks in. You have to wrap the handler in useCallback as well — and for a list, the renderItem function too.*
> *These days React Compiler handles most of this automatically at build time, so a lot of the manual useCallback noise can go away. But it optimises within a component. Things like cache timing or list virtualisation are still design decisions I have to make."*

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `shallow comparison` | so sánh nông | *A shallow comparison of all props.* |
| `kick in` | bắt đầu có tác dụng | *Memo never kicks in.* |
| `leave it alone` | để yên, không đụng vào | *Otherwise I leave it alone.* |
| `a fraction of` | một phần nhỏ của | *A fraction of a millisecond.* |
| `noise` (n) | code thừa gây nhiễu | *A lot of the manual noise can go away.* |

